WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
A country house, 1773.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.360
A young gentleman thinks it's an
inn, and orders the owner about.

3
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.820
London, 1895.

4
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:14.040
A grand lady with a notebook
questions a nervous young suitor.

5
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:17.850
Later, at a garden tea, one
young woman tells another:

6
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.740
"When I see a spade I call it a spade."

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.780
The whole theatre is laughing.

8
00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.450
But what is the joke really aimed at?

9
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.020
In this mission, you'll
learn the genre's tools,

10
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.390
from wit to the marriage market.

11
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.170
You'll catch a young man with two
completely different sets of manners,

12
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.000
and ask what switches them.

13
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.830
And you'll take apart a famous
line about losing two parents,

14
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.050
to see how the joke is built.

15
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.720
Your mission: work out what
the joke is really aimed at.
